# 1. THE NON-NEGOTIABLE PRODUCT GOAL

ANATOMY 360 must eventually provide a comprehensive educational foundation for people studying human biology, anatomy, biomedical sciences, medicine, allied health and clinical sciences.

The platform should support six relevant academic tracks:

1. School Foundations (Grades 6–8).
2. Secondary / Pre-Medical (Grades 9–12, Matric, FSc, O/A-Level, AP and equivalent).
3. Medical Foundations (MBBS, MD and equivalent pre-clinical education).
4. Clinical & Applied Medicine.
5. Allied Health (nursing and other allied-health programmes).
6. Graduate / BS / MPhil / PhD Research.

Content must be written at an appropriate academic depth.

A school student should not be presented with unnecessarily complicated medical terminology without an explanation.

An MBBS student should not receive only a school-level introduction.

An advanced student should have access to mechanisms, quantitative concepts, research context and deeper references where appropriate.

The objective is not to claim that ANATOMY 360 contains every fact ever published in medicine.

The objective is to complete a clearly defined, evidence-based core human-sciences curriculum, with all of its required learning outcomes addressed and its material gaps honestly recorded.

## Completion means actual educational coverage.

A subject with 20 empty chapter records is not complete.

A subject with 20 introductory paragraphs is not complete.

A subject with 20 YouTube links but no written teaching material is not complete.

A subject with 20 textbook references but no topic-specific explanation is not complete.

A subject with 20 diagrams but no explanation of what they show is not complete.

Every chapter and topic must have a meaningful learning package.

