# 4. REQUIRED EDUCATIONAL PACKAGE FOR EVERY TOPIC

This section is mandatory.

Every topic must receive its own educational package, connected to its parent chapter and domain.

Do not create a generic resource list for an entire domain and pretend all its topics are supported.

## 4.1 Complete written learning material

Every topic must have a substantive original teaching explanation.

Where appropriate, the content should contain:

1. Topic introduction.
2. Clear learning objectives.
3. Required prerequisite knowledge.
4. Key definitions.
5. Main concepts.
6. Mechanisms and processes.
7. Step-by-step explanations.
8. Important structures or components.
9. Functional relationships.
10. Relevant examples.
11. Diagrams or tables.
12. Common misconceptions.
13. Clinical or applied correlations.
14. Topic summary.
15. Key takeaways.
16. Self-assessment questions.
17. References.

The lesson must be long enough to teach the actual defined learning outcomes.

Do not use artificial word-count padding.

Do not produce a single paragraph for a subject that requires multiple chapters.

## 4.2 Academic depth

Write different explanations appropriate to the six tracks.

Do not simply duplicate the same paragraph under six academic labels.

Where a topic does not apply to a given track, identify the appropriate tracks instead of forcing irrelevant material into that level.

Medical and graduate-level content must include appropriate mechanisms, terminology, quantitative explanations and deeper references.

## 4.3 Separate external reading links

Every chapter must have a dedicated reading collection.

Target:
- At least one primary textbook or comprehensive learning source.
- At least one supplementary source.
- Additional subject-specific references when required.

Every link must be connected to the relevant chapter and topic.

Store:
- Resource title.
- Author or publisher.
- Exact URL.
- Chapter or section covered.
- Academic level.
- Language.
- Access type.
- Licence or access restrictions.
- Date checked.
- Topic relationship.
- Review status.

Do not link only to a publisher homepage when a precise chapter link exists.

