10. Do not fabricate images, scientific data, research findings or academic references.
11. Do not create false faculty-review labels.
12. Do not present generated content as formally approved medical teaching material.
13. Never fabricate external URLs.
14. Never label unavailable resources as available.
15. Every factual medical explanation must be cross-checked against appropriate credible sources.

For clinical and pharmacological subjects, use up-to-date references and clearly state that the platform is for education, not individual diagnosis or prescribing.

